WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.069 --> 00:00:05.730
Pixar is renowned for cramming loads of Easter
Eggs and references into their animations,

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:11.110
so with Inside Out on Blu-ray and DVD now,
I wanted to take a look at my top 10 Easter

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:12.809
Eggs in Pixar's 15th feature film.

00:00:12.809 --> 00:00:16.970
And for those of you who've been desperately
searching for the 3 times that director Pete

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:21.699
Docter says the Pizza Planet Truck appears
in the movie, I've found them all!

00:00:21.699 --> 00:00:24.060
Keep watching to find out where they are!

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:29.289
Ok, kicking off with number 10, remember the
Married Life montage at the start of Up?

00:00:29.289 --> 00:00:33.620
Well, that movie was also directed by Inside
Out's Pete Docter and there are several nice

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:35.250
nods to it in this movie.

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:39.329
They're tricky to spot as they can be kind
of blurred, but you can see several of Carl's

00:00:39.329 --> 00:00:44.899
ties in a number of memory balls at Headquarters,
and Carl's face also pops up in a green memory

00:00:44.899 --> 00:00:50.030
ball in the Long-Term Memory storage area,
and you can also see Carl with Ellie in several

00:00:50.030 --> 00:00:54.310
more memory balls behind Joy, Sadness and
Riley's imaginary friend Bing Bong.

00:00:54.310 --> 00:01:00.039
At number 9, When a young Riley jumps between
sofas pretending the lounge floor is covered

00:01:00.039 --> 00:01:04.390
in lava, take a look at the table and you'll
see a magazine with a cover featuring Colette

00:01:04.390 --> 00:01:05.390
from Ratatouille!

00:01:05.390 --> 00:01:10.040
Moving on to number 8, you probably noticed
the girl in Riley's class wearing a similar

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:13.070
top to Sid's skull t-shirt in Toy Story.

00:01:13.070 --> 00:01:18.070
But according to Pixar, one of the boys in
Riley's class is also wearing a camouflage-patterned

00:01:18.070 --> 00:01:20.840
top that's made up of Toy Story characters!

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:27.570
If you look really carefully, you can see
what looks like T-rex, Woody, and possibly

00:01:27.570 --> 00:01:30.299
Hamm and the bottom of Mr Potato Head.

00:01:30.299 --> 00:01:35.250
Oh, and the globe in Riley's classroom also
appeared in the Toy Story movies, and we also

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:38.790
see it at the end of this movie in the mind
of Riley's new teacher.

00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:44.530
At number 7, as well as shout-outs to past
Pixar movies, Inside Out includes an Easter

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:48.790
Egg looking forward to Pixar's 16th feature
film, The Good Dinosaur.

00:01:48.790 --> 00:01:54.380
A statue that looks rather like Forrest Woodbush,
a Styracosaurus from The Good Dinosaur, appears

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:57.979
in Riley's memory of her family's journey
to San Francisco.

00:01:57.979 --> 00:02:02.520
And the family's car rolls into the back of
a dino-statue that could well be a nod to

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:04.430
Arlo, the star of The Good Dinosaur!

00:02:04.430 --> 00:02:09.840
And at number 6, when Joy, Sadness and Bing
Bong head into Imagination Land, there's a

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:14.080
stack of board games including one called
"Find Me!", which features a picture of a

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:18.510
clownfish on the box, a clear shout-out to
Pixar's Finding Nemo.

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:23.120
And under that game, there's another called
"Dinosaur World", a little nod to The Good

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:24.120
Dinosaur.

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:28.270
Plus, there's a board game named after Pixar's
short film, "For The Birds", and those same

00:02:28.270 --> 00:02:33.270
birds from that short also appear during Riley's
journey to San Francisco.

00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:38.390
In at number 5, there are two scenes in Imagination
Land in which first Bing Bong and later Joy

00:02:38.390 --> 00:02:41.330
make a Cloud person disappear into thin air.

00:02:41.330 --> 00:02:45.030
The second time it happens, one police officer
tells his colleague who wants to pursue the

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:50.040
culprit, "Forget it, Jake; it's Cloudtown",
which is a funny reference to director Roman

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:55.700
Polanski's 1970s movie Chinatown, which starred
Jack Nicholson, and ended with Nicholson's

00:02:55.700 --> 00:02:58.930
private investigator character being told,
"Forget it, Jake.

00:02:58.930 --> 00:02:59.930
It's Chinatown."

00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:04.940
At number 4, the director at Dream Productions,
the place where Riley's dreams and nightmares

00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:09.680
are created, gives the order to "add the reality
distortion filter" to the camera, which is

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:13.840
a nod to Apple co-founder and former Pixar
CEO Steve Jobs.

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:19.610
An original member of the Apple Mac design
team said Jobs had a "reality distortion field",

00:03:19.610 --> 00:03:24.740
which basically meant reality was like putty
in his hands and he could convince anyone

00:03:24.740 --> 00:03:26.720
of anything.

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:32.370
Similarly, the "reality distortion filter"
in Inside Out alters what the actors bringing

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:34.600
to life Riley's dream look like.

00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:39.090
At number 3, one of the stores that Riley
and her mum walk past in San Francisco is

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:44.340
a Locksmith called Krause, which is named
after Inside Out's supervising animator Shawn

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:45.340
Krause.

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:49.450
Did you also notice the poster at the bottom
right-hand corner of the store window?

00:03:49.450 --> 00:03:55.620
It says "Sure Locks For Homes Special", which
sounds rather like "Sherlock Holmes Special",

00:03:55.620 --> 00:03:57.700
and not only is there a new special episode
of TV's Sherlock coming up, but Pixar has

00:03:57.700 --> 00:03:59.510
its own connection to Sherlock.

00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:03.540
Pixar's Chief Creative Officer John Lasseter
previously worked on the live-action film

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:08.860
Young Sherlock Holmes, which was ground-breaking
for his animation of a fully computer-generated

00:04:08.860 --> 00:04:09.860
character.

00:04:09.860 --> 00:04:14.870
In at number 2, when Bing Bong, Joy and Sadness
arrive at Dream Productions, Bing Bong points

00:04:14.870 --> 00:04:18.600
out a poster for "I Can Fly!", a dream he
says he loves.

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:24.100
That poster is a little nod to Disney's 1953
animated feature film, Peter Pan, which Pete

00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:28.720
Docter has said was an influence on Inside
Out, and it also happened to feature a song

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:29.930
titled "You Can Fly!"

00:04:29.930 --> 00:04:35.120
And the poster alongside that for the dream
"I'm Falling For A Very Long Time Into A Pit"

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:40.150
is very reminiscent of the poster that designer
Saul Bass created for Alfred Hitchcock's movie

00:04:40.150 --> 00:04:41.150
Vertigo.

00:04:41.150 --> 00:04:46.850
And in the top spot at number one, director
Pete Docter said that Pixar's Easter Egg regular,

00:04:46.850 --> 00:04:51.430
the Pizza Planet Truck, appears three times
in Inside Out, but that it's really difficult

00:04:51.430 --> 00:04:52.430
to spot.

00:04:52.430 --> 00:04:53.430
And he wasn't kidding!

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:55.380
But I've found all three appearances!

00:04:55.380 --> 00:04:59.730
Well, actually, it appears four times in three
scenes!

00:04:59.730 --> 00:05:03.650
It first appears in one of the memory balls
that rolls along the floor when Joy first

00:05:03.650 --> 00:05:05.980
sees Riley's imaginary friend Bing Bong.

00:05:05.980 --> 00:05:10.410
The second one pops up as Riley starts to
play ice hockey; and then it appears again

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:15.910
for a third time when Anger explodes after
Riley falls down during that same hockey game.

00:05:15.910 --> 00:05:19.810
The last one makes an appearance when Joy,
Sadness, and Bing Bong are on the Train Of

00:05:19.810 --> 00:05:23.400
Thought � in fact, Bing Bong even handles
it for a moment!

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:28.850
Of course, I also loved seeing other Pixar
regulars like A113, which makes an appearance

00:05:28.850 --> 00:05:33.780
when Riley runs away from home, and the Luxo
Ball, which turns up during Riley's playtime

00:05:33.780 --> 00:05:34.780
with Bing Bong.

00:05:34.780 --> 00:05:38.700
But, what other Easter eggs and references
did you spot in Inside Out?

00:05:38.700 --> 00:05:40.360
And which are your favourites?

